override_flags_definitions is not gated by the internal token check
Any external caller with a valid project API token can include override_flags_definitions in the request body and replace a flag's conditions with arbitrary definitions — for example, forcing a flag to 100% rollout with no property conditions. This bypasses feature gate logic for the caller's own evaluation. detailed_analysis is correctly gated behind is_internal_request, but the override field is wired through unconditionally.
let override_defs = if authentication::is_internal_request(&context) {
    request.override_flags_definitions.as_ref()
} else {
    None
};
let filtered_flags = flags::fetch_and_filter(
    &flag_service,
    team.id,
    &context.meta,
    &context.headers,
    request.evaluation_runtime,
    request.evaluation_contexts.as_ref(),
    override_defs,
)
.await?;
