blocking: serde_json::from_value::<FeatureFlag>(override_def.clone()) parses the entire flag struct, including id and team_id, and then *flag = override_flag replaces it wholesale. The override is keyed by flag_key only, so a caller can submit override_flags_definitions = {"my-flag": {"id": 999, "team_id": 999, ...}} and the runtime evaluates against team 999's id space. Downstream rollout bucketing, cohort lookup, and the canonical log all read from the swapped struct.
INTERNAL_REQUEST_TOKEN gating limits exposure today (only test_evaluation calls this), but Copilot already flagged this on the PR and the assertion is cheap. Better to land it now before this endpoint grows other callers.
